   "created": 1793002829,
   "author": "Peter M. M.",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/petermmoricz_jane-street-and-rivals-are-now-fighting-for-activity-7520398938034589697-Aej_",
   "text": "Wall Street's speed traders go all in on AI.\nFor years, Jane Street, Hudson River Trading and their rivals fought over every nanosecond. Now they're also fighting for compute, the raw processing power behind AI.\n\nThe spending surge\n- One executive estimates market makers now spend 10 to 20 times more on compute than before ChatGPT launched.\n- Hudson River spends about $1 billion a year on AI, and that figure is rising.\n- Jane Street took a $1 billion stake in CoreWeave and pledged $6 billion in compute spending with it, plus a $13 billion deal with Crusoe.\n\nBuilding their own data centers\n- Hudson River runs part of its processing inside a former mine in a Norwegian mountain, cooled by fjord",
