  "7520512935694290944": {
   "created": 1793030008,
   "author": "Ada Offonry",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/activity-7520512935694290944-4Q4T",
   "text": "Why are market makers spending 10-20 times more on Compute than before ChatGPT launched?\n\nEspecially when people like Ken Griffin say that AI is almost certainly in a bubble.\n\nDespite his views, Ken's market maker, Citadel Securities, keeps scaling up its use of AI chips.\n\nThe rest of the industry is doing the same. \n\nFor years, market makers competed on speed. \n\nNow they also compete on compute.\n\nThe money goes 3 ways:\n\n1. Cloud partnerships. Hudson River Trading signed a multi year deal with CoreWeave  and spends about $1bn a year on AI.\n\n2. Investments. Jane Street bought a $1bn stake in CoreWeave and led the round that valued chip startup Etched at $21bn.\n\n3. Building out their own data ",
